            <ArticleTitle>Ruthenium-Catalyzed meta-Carboxylation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6662-6665</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03387</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The meta-carboxylation of arenes containing pyridine and other azine-directing groups is reported. Using carbon tetrabromide as the C1 source, ruthenium(III) trichloride catalysis enables functionalization of the arene meta-C-H position, affording carboxy methyl ester products after in situ reaction with methanol.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
